<title>POLAND: Polish 91-day NBP-bill avg yield up to 22.17 pct.</title>
<headline>Polish 91-day NBP-bill avg yield up to 22.17 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland raised the average yield of its 91-day bill to 22.17 percent from 22.15 percent at the last auction, selling 22 million zlotys of the paper against a 200 million offer.</p>
<p>The NBP also rejected all 10-million worth of bids at its 100 million zloty reverse repo offer. At the last such operation the maximum accepted drainage rate was 22.15 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
